---
// Literal recreation of the Claude Design canvas's Admin Products screen.
// No distinct "AdminProducts.dc.html" artboard exists in the design
// export (same situation as every other Admin screen so far) — the
// ground truth is project/PageProducts.dc.html's own `role="admin"`
// branch, composed into the established Admin shell: NavSidebar
// role="admin" + the plain shared NavTop.astro (section="Inventory",
// matching ADMIN_NAV's own "Inventory" group label — the same section
// name the sibling /inventory/products screen already uses for this
// exact same design). project/StaffLookup.dc.html's own role="staff"
// composition (already built as /inventory/products/index.astro) proved
// the real query/derivation techniques reused below — same real
// products/categories/inventory data, same real supplier-from-restock
// derivation, same real stock-status computation — just with the design's
// genuinely different isAdmin column set (Cost/Price/Margin, not
// Location·bin/Supplier-as-column) and admin-specific real capabilities
// layered on top.
//
// ROUTE REUSE / SHELL WARNING: /inventory/products/new.astro and
// /inventory/products/[id].astro are real, still-functioning product
// create/edit forms (inventory_staff/admin/super_admin genuinely retain
// products_insert_staff/products_update_staff RLS) — but they render the
// OLD AppShell/DESIGN.md visual system, not this Claude Design shell.
// Per your explicit "do not reuse Sales/Inventory page markup" and
// "Admin shell experience" instructions, and the same wrong-shell
// reasoning already applied throughout this project (Inventory Staff's
// Support Tickets, Admin Customers' preview panel, Admin Sales Orders'
// New order button before Admin New Order existed), this screen does NOT
// link to either of those old-shell forms. Same for /inventory/categories
// (also real, also old-shell) — not linked to either.
//
// CREATE / EDIT SCOPE: the design's "New product" button and each
// product-name link both point to a single "AdminProductDetail" screen
// (detailHref) that serves as both the create form and the edit/view
// screen — that screen is explicitly out of scope this turn ("Do not
// implement: Admin Product Info"). Building a full inline create/edit
// form directly on this list screen instead would be inventing that same
// screen under a different name, so — same precedent as Admin Sales
// Orders' "New order" button and order-id link before Admin Order
// Detail/Admin New Order existed — both are OMITTED this turn, not routed
// anywhere fake, and will become real once Admin Product Info is
// approved. "Manage categories" is omitted for the identical reason
// (genuine category CRUD exists, but only via the old-shell
// /inventory/categories UI — building a new Admin-shell category
// subsystem is explicitly out of scope: "otherwise do not create a new
// category-management subsystem in this turn," and no Claude Design
// screen for it exists in this project's 13-screen list either).
//
// DELETE SCOPE: unlike create/edit, delete needs no form — a real,
// role-correct delete action was wired directly into this screen's own
// row-actions slot (no new screen needed), reusing the exact same
// backend Admin Order Detail's cancel/refund controls already proved:
// super_admin gets the real, direct `deleteProduct` Action (real
// products_delete_super_admin RLS); admin gets the real
// `requestApproval({actionType:'delete_product'})` flow (Phase 9's
// existing approval workflow — admin is already one of the five
// action-type-authorized requester roles for delete_product). Neither
// role gets more than it already has — admin was NEVER given direct
// delete, exactly preserving products_delete_super_admin's existing
// boundary. create_approval_request()'s own real validation (rejects a
// product with any order_items/inventory_movements history, rejects a
// duplicate pending request) surfaces its real error message unchanged.
//
// Real vs deferred/fabricated, per your explicit no-fabrication rules:
//  - Real: SKU, name, real category (categories join), real price, real
//    cost (nullable — "—" shown honestly when absent, same as the design
//    admin branch would need for any product without a recorded cost),
//    real Margin (only computed when cost is present — (price−cost)/price,
//    never fabricated when cost is null), real inventory on-hand, real
//    reorder level ("Low at"), real stock-status pill (In stock/Low/Out —
//    identical qty<=reorder_level computation used everywhere else in
//    this project), real category tabs with real counts, real name/SKU
//    search, real "Status" facet (in/low/out — same real facet mapping
//    already proven on /inventory/products, not repurposed to mean
//    something else), real "Supplier" facet (same real most-recent-
//    restock derivation already proven on /inventory/products — the only
//    place a supplier is ever actually attached to a product in this
//    schema).
//  - Admin-specific real addition beyond the sibling staff/sales screens:
//    this screen shows the FULL real catalog (active AND inactive), not
//    just active products — products_select_staff RLS already grants
//    admin (and every staff role) unscoped product visibility regardless
//    of is_active; /sales/products and /inventory/products simply choose
//    not to exercise that for their own read-only/lookup purposes. A
//    small real "Inactive" tag renders next to the product name only when
//    is_active is false (0 real rows currently exercise this, but the
//    field and its real value are genuinely used, not fabricated).
//  - Product name now links to the real /admin/products/[id] (Admin
//    Product Info, built in a later turn) — previously plain text while
//    that screen didn't exist yet.
//  - "New product" button, "Manage categories": still omitted — see
//    CREATE / EDIT SCOPE / DELETE SCOPE above (unchanged this turn).
//  - "Import" header action: admin-only in the design, but no real bulk-
//    import capability exists anywhere in this app — omitted, not
//    invented (same precedent as Admin Customers' own "Import" button).
//  - Row checkboxes + any bulk action: no real bulk product action exists
//    — omitted (same "do not invent bulk actions" precedent as every
//    other Admin list screen).
//  - "..." row-actions dots: replaced with the one real action this
//    schema and RLS actually support per-row without a new screen —
//    Delete/Request deletion (see DELETE SCOPE above) — not a fake menu.
//  - "View" grid/list toggle, pagination footer ("Page 1 of 380"): no
//    view-mode or pagination capability exists — omitted, replaced with a
//    real "{N} of {M} products" count, same precedent as every other
//    Admin/Sales/Staff list screen.
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import NavSidebar from "../../../components/staff/NavSidebar.astro";
import NavTop from "../../../components/staff/NavTop.astro";

const url = Astro.url;
const search = url.searchParams.get("search")?.trim() ?? "";
const category = url.searchParams.get("category") ?? "";
const status = url.searchParams.get("status") ?? "";
const supplier = url.searchParams.get("supplier") ?? "";
const viewerRole = (Astro.locals.role === "super_admin" ? "super_admin" : "admin") as "admin" | "super_admin";

// --- Real full catalog (active AND inactive — see header comment) ---
const { data: productRows } = await Astro.locals.supabase
  .from("products")
  .select("id, sku, name, price, cost, is_active, category_id, categories(name), inventory(quantity_on_hand, reorder_level)")
  .order("name");

// Real "most recent restock supplier" per product — identical derivation
// already proven on /inventory/products.
const { data: restockRows } = await Astro.locals.supabase
  .from("inventory_movements")
  .select("product_id, created_at, suppliers(name)")
  .eq("movement_type", "restock")
  .not("supplier_id", "is", null)
  .order("created_at", { ascending: false });

const supplierByProduct = new Map<string, string>();
for (const r of restockRows ?? []) {
  if (supplierByProduct.has(r.product_id as string)) continue;
  const name = (r.suppliers as unknown as { name: string } | null)?.name;
  if (name) supplierByProduct.set(r.product_id as string, name);
}

function categoryOf(row: { categories: unknown }): { name: string } | null {
  return row.categories as unknown as { name: string } | null;
}
function inventoryOf(row: { inventory: unknown }): { quantity_on_hand: number; reorder_level: number } | null {
  const inv = row.inventory as unknown as { quantity_on_hand: number; reorder_level: number }[] | null;
  return inv?.[0] ?? null;
}

const formatCurrency = (value: number) =>
  new Intl.NumberFormat("en-IN", { style: "currency", currency: "INR", maximumFractionDigits: 2 }).format(value);

const allProducts = (productRows ?? []).map((p) => {
  const inv = inventoryOf(p);
  const qty = inv?.quantity_on_hand ?? 0;
  const reorderLevel = inv?.reorder_level ?? 0;
  const stockTone: "in" | "low" | "out" = qty === 0 ? "out" : qty <= reorderLevel ? "low" : "in";
  const cost = p.cost === null ? null : Number(p.cost);
  const price = Number(p.price);
  const margin = cost !== null && price > 0 ? Math.round(((price - cost) / price) * 100) : null;
  return {
    id: p.id,
    sku: p.sku,
    name: p.name,
    isActive: p.is_active,
    categoryId: p.category_id as string | null,
    categoryName: categoryOf(p)?.name ?? "Uncategorised",
    price,
    cost,
    margin,
    qty,
    reorderLevel,
    stockTone,
    supplier: supplierByProduct.get(p.id) ?? null,
  };
});

const STOCK_LABEL: Record<string, string> = { in: "In stock", low: "Low stock", out: "Out of stock" };

// Real category tabs (counts over the full real catalog, unaffected by
// search/status/supplier — same convention as /inventory/products).
const categoryCounts = new Map<string, { name: string; count: number }>();
for (const p of allProducts) {
  if (!p.categoryId) continue;
  const existing = categoryCounts.get(p.categoryId);
  if (existing) existing.count += 1;
  else categoryCounts.set(p.categoryId, { name: p.categoryName, count: 1 });
}
const categoryTabs = [...categoryCounts.entries()]
  .map(([id, v]) => ({ id, name: v.name, count: v.count }))
  .sort((a, b) => a.name.localeCompare(b.name));

const STATUS_OPTIONS = [
  { value: "", label: "All statuses" },
  { value: "in", label: "In stock" },
  { value: "low", label: "Low stock" },
  { value: "out", label: "Out of stock" },
];

const supplierOptions = [...new Set(allProducts.map((p) => p.supplier).filter((s): s is string => !!s))].sort((a, b) =>
  a.localeCompare(b)
);

const filtered = allProducts.filter((p) => {
  if (category && p.categoryId !== category) return false;
  if (status && p.stockTone !== status) return false;
  if (supplier && p.supplier !== supplier) return false;
  if (!search) return true;
  const needle = search.toLowerCase();
  return p.name.toLowerCase().includes(needle) || p.sku.toLowerCase().includes(needle);
});

function buildUrl(overrides: Record<string, string | undefined>) {
  const next = new URLSearchParams(url.search);
  for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(overrides)) {
    if (value) next.set(key, value);
    else next.delete(key);
  }
  const qs = next.toString();
  return qs ? `/admin/products?${qs}` : "/admin/products";
}

// --- Real subtitle stats (independent of the current search/filter) ---
const lowOnStockCount = allProducts.filter((p) => p.stockTone === "low" || p.stockTone === "out").length;
---

<BaseLayout title="Products — Admin">
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="sd" id="sd-root">
    <div id="sd-sidebar-backdrop" class="sd__backdrop"></div>

    <div id="sd-sidebar" class="sd__sidebar">
      <NavSidebar active="Products" role="admin" viewerRole={viewerRole} />
    </div>

    <div class="sd__panel">
      <NavTop section="Inventory" page="Products" searchAction="/admin/products" searchName="search" searchValue={search} searchPlaceholder="Filter by name or SKU…" />

      <main id="main-content" class="ap__main">
        <div class="ap__header">
          <div class="ap__heading-col">
            <h1>Products</h1>
            <span class="ap__subtitle">{allProducts.length} SKU{allProducts.length === 1 ? "" : "s"} in {categoryTabs.length} categor{categoryTabs.length === 1 ? "y" : "ies"} · {lowOnStockCount} low on stock</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="ap__toolbar">
          <div role="tablist" aria-label="Category" class="ap__tabs">
            <a href={buildUrl({ category: undefined })} role="tab" aria-selected={!category} class={!category ? "is-active" : ""}>
              All <span class="ap__tab-count">{allProducts.length}</span>
            </a>
            {categoryTabs.map((t) => (
              <a href={buildUrl({ category: t.id })} role="tab" aria-selected={category === t.id} class={category === t.id ? "is-active" : ""}>
                {t.name} <span class="ap__tab-count">{t.count}</span>
              </a>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="ap__toolbar">
          <select id="ap-status-filter" class="ap__facet-select" aria-label="Filter by status">
            {STATUS_OPTIONS.map((o) => (
              <option value={buildUrl({ status: o.value || undefined })} selected={status === o.value}>
                {o.value ? o.label : "+ Status"}
              </option>
            ))}
          </select>
          <select id="ap-supplier-filter" class="ap__facet-select" aria-label="Filter by supplier">
            <option value={buildUrl({ supplier: undefined })} selected={!supplier}>+ Supplier</option>
            {supplierOptions.map((s) => (
              <option value={buildUrl({ supplier: s })} selected={supplier === s}>{s}</option>
            ))}
          </select>
        </div>

        {
          filtered.length > 0 ? (
            <div class="ap__panel">
              <div class="ap__grid ap__grid-head">
                <span>Product</span>
                <span>Category</span>
                <span class="ap__col-right">Cost</span>
                <span class="ap__col-right">Price</span>
                <span class="ap__col-right">Margin</span>
                <span class="ap__col-right">On hand</span>
                <span class="ap__col-right">Low at</span>
                <span>Status</span>
                <span></span>
              </div>
              {filtered.map((p) => (
                <div class="ap__grid ap__row">
                  <div class="ap__product-cell">
                    <span class="ap__product-icon">
                      <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 7.5 12 3l9 4.5v9L12 21l-9-4.5zM3 7.5 12 12l9-4.5M12 12v9" /></svg>
                    </span>
                    <a href={`/admin/products/${p.id}`} class="ap__product-name-col">
                      <span class="ap__product-name-row">
                        <span class="ap__product-name">{p.name}</span>
                        {!p.isActive && <span class="ap__inactive-tag">Inactive</span>}
                      </span>
                      <span class="ap__product-sku">{p.sku}</span>
                    </a>
                  </div>
                  <span class="ap__muted-cell">{p.categoryName}</span>
                  <span class="ap__col-right ap__muted-cell">{p.cost !== null ? formatCurrency(p.cost) : "—"}</span>
                  <span class="ap__col-right ap__price-cell">{formatCurrency(p.price)}</span>
                  <span class="ap__col-right ap__muted-cell">{p.margin !== null ? `${p.margin}%` : "—"}</span>
                  <span class="ap__col-right ap__on-hand">{p.qty}</span>
                  <span class="ap__col-right ap__muted-cell">{p.reorderLevel}</span>
                  <span>
                    <span class={`ap__pill ap__pill--${p.stockTone}`}>{STOCK_LABEL[p.stockTone]}</span>
                  </span>
                  <span class="ap__row-action">
                    {viewerRole === "super_admin" ? (
                      <button type="button" class="ap__delete-btn" data-action="delete-direct" data-product-id={p.id} data-product-name={p.name}>
                        Delete
                      </button>
                    ) : (
                      <button type="button" class="ap__delete-btn" data-action="delete-request" data-product-id={p.id} data-product-name={p.name}>
                        Request deletion
                      </button>
                    )}
                  </span>
                </div>
              ))}
              <div class="ap__panel-footer">
                <span class="ap__panel-footer-count">{filtered.length} of {allProducts.length} product{allProducts.length === 1 ? "" : "s"}</span>
                <p id="ap-row-message" class="ap__row-message" role="status" />
              </div>
            </div>
          ) : (
            <div class="ap__empty">
              <p class="ap__empty-title">No products found</p>
              <p class="ap__empty-body">Try a different search or filter.</p>
            </div>
          )
        }
      </main>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
